# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Dependencies
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Rust
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Build output (Cargo.lock IS tracked for reproducible CI)
/target

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Web SPA (CASTCU-S1-T08)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Generated wasm copy fed to Vite — rebuilt by `npm run build:wasm`.
web/src/wasm/*.wasm
# Vite build output baked into the server's rust-embed folder. The hashed
# `assets/` bundle is a build product (never committed); the placeholder
# index.html stays TRACKED as the compile-time baseline (restored post-build).
crates/asciicut-server/web/assets/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Tauri desktop shell (CASTCU-S2-T01)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Dedicated desktop SPA build fed to Tauri's `frontendDist` — a build product.
# (Also matched by the unanchored `dist/` above; listed explicitly for clarity.)
web/dist/
# The detached desktop crate's build output. The root `/target` ignore is
# anchored, so this nested target dir needs its own entry. The crate's icons/
# and its own Cargo.lock stay TRACKED (reproducible bundling).
crates/asciicut-desktop/target/
# Tauri codegen output (capability/permission schemas) — regenerated per build.
crates/asciicut-desktop/gen/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sample / render artifacts
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `castcut compose` / `POST /api/export` emit `<stem>.composed.cast` next to the
# source — a build product, not a fixture.
samples/*.composed.cast
# render artifacts (export output) — never commit video/image exports
*.gif
*.mp4
*.webm
*.png
!samples/**/*.png
# Tauri desktop app icons ARE committed (bundle.icon in tauri.conf.json needs
# them for `tauri build`) — re-include them after the blanket `*.png` ignore.
!crates/asciicut-desktop/icons/*.png
# Nibbles brand assets (logomark, mascot, empty/loading illustrations, animated
# splice-operator gif) ARE committed — the SPA loads them at runtime from
# /assets, and `assets/` is the source of record. Re-include after the blanket
# `*.png`/`*.gif` ignores.
!assets/*.png
!web/public/assets/*.png
!assets/*.gif
!web/public/assets/*.gif
# README demo screencast (app in use) + rendered edit output live in assets/.
!assets/*.mp4

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OS / editor
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
*.log
.idea/
.vscode/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Python prototype
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Grove (code-indexing / tree-sitter grammars)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Grammar WASM binaries are cached GLOBALLY (~/.cache/grove/grammars), never
# inside the repo, so there is no grove-transient path to ignore here.
# The grove project files ARE tracked (do not ignore):
#   .grove/config.json  — per-project grove config (harnesses, mode)
#   grove.lock          — pinned grammar versions + sha256, like Cargo.lock

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Forge (sprint/task/bug management)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Transient runtime artifacts — do NOT commit:
#   context/persona packs, preflight status, run-task debug logs
.forge/cache/
#   per-task orchestrator transcripts
.forge/transcripts/
#   one JSON per phase event (runtime telemetry)
.forge/store/events/
#   collation timestamp/state (regenerated by /forge:collate)
.forge/store/COLLATION_STATE.json
#   enhancement staging working dir
.forge/enhancements/
#   version-check cache
.forge/update-check-cache.json
#
# Everything else under .forge/ IS tracked project infrastructure:
#   .forge/config.json  schemas/  templates/  workflows/  personas/  skills/
#   tools/  mcp/  meta/  init/  .base-pack/  *-manifest.json  init-context.*
#   pi-settings.json  project-context.json  structure-versions.json
#   .forge/store/{sprints,tasks,bugs,features}/  — source-of-truth JSON records

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pi / Claude local overrides
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.pi/pi-claude-compat/
# Local (personal) Claude Code settings — shared settings.json stays tracked.
.claude/settings.local.json
# Allow tracking the manual documentation landing page files
!/docs/
/docs/*
!/docs/index.html
!/docs/style.css
!/docs/styles.css
!/docs/script.js
!/docs/assets/
!/docs/assets/**
